\ Fast synthetic test for the exhaustive year-candidate enumeration.
\ Eleven invented gates are six hundred days apart, numbered -3..7.
\ Foundation is gate zero, and the calculation day equals Foundation.
\ There are exactly eleven eligible (opening, closing] year pairs
\ with at least six intervals and no more than 5778 days.
\ The first three choices have length 3600 and opening indices -3,-2,-1.
\ The fourth has length 4200 and opening index -3.
\ The last has length 5400 and opening index -2.
\ No sauce calculation is needed for this synthetic sorting test.

To add a synthetic gate given a number and a calendar day:
  Put the number into the gate walk's current index.
  Put the calendar day into the gate walk's current position.
  Record a positive gate mark.

To make synthetic year gates:
  Destroy the nearby gate ledger.
  Add a synthetic gate given -3 and -15057471.
  Add a synthetic gate given -2 and -15056871.
  Add a synthetic gate given -1 and -15056271.
  Add a synthetic gate given 0 and -15055671.
  Add a synthetic gate given 1 and -15055071.
  Add a synthetic gate given 2 and -15054471.
  Add a synthetic gate given 3 and -15053871.
  Add a synthetic gate given 4 and -15053271.
  Add a synthetic gate given 5 and -15052671.
  Add a synthetic gate given 6 and -15052071.
  Add a synthetic gate given 7 and -15051471.
  Put -15055671 into the year selection day.

To check the year 5000 candidate enumeration:
  Make synthetic year gates.
  Gather eligible year candidates.
  If the eligible year count is not 11,
    put "Synthetic year enumeration did not find eleven pairs." into the check report; exit.
  Put 1 into the selected year rank.
  Read the selected year candidate.
  If the chosen year's opening index is not -3,
    put "First candidate did not open at gate -3." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's closing index is not 3,
    put "First candidate did not close at gate 3." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's year length is not 3600,
    put "First candidate does not have the shortest length." into the check report; exit.
  Put 2 into the selected year rank.
  Read the selected year candidate.
  If the chosen year's opening index is not -2,
    put "Second candidate did not open at gate -2." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's closing index is not 4,
    put "Second candidate did not close at gate 4." into the check report; exit.
  Put 3 into the selected year rank.
  Read the selected year candidate.
  If the chosen year's opening index is not -1,
    put "Third candidate did not open at gate -1." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's closing index is not 5,
    put "Third candidate did not close at gate 5." into the check report; exit.
  Put 4 into the selected year rank.
  Read the selected year candidate.
  If the chosen year's year length is not 4200,
    put "Fourth candidate did not begin the next length group." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's opening index is not -3,
    put "Fourth candidate tie break did not choose gate -3." into the check report; exit.
  Put 11 into the selected year rank.
  Read the selected year candidate.
  If the chosen year's opening index is not -2,
    put "Last candidate did not open at gate -2." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's closing index is not 7,
    put "Last candidate did not close at gate 7." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's year length is not 5400,
    put "Last candidate had the wrong maximum eligible length." into the check report; exit.
  Destroy the eligible year ledger.
  Destroy the nearby gate ledger.

\ This is a much slower integration check, using the actual gate sauce.
\ It is intentionally NOT part of the ordinary short test sequence.
\ After a real CAL run it should locate exactly the historical
\ Foundation-Day year-5000 interval recorded in the main README.
To check the complete Foundation year 5000:
  Find year 5000 for -15055671.
  If the year selection success is not 1,
    put "The Foundation year 5000 was not selected." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's opening day is not -15057703,
    put "Year 5000 has an incorrect opening gate." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's closing day is not -15053459,
    put "Year 5000 has an incorrect closing gate." into the check report; exit.
  If the chosen year's year length is not 4244,
    put "Year 5000 has an incorrect duration." into the check report; exit.
